+# Async Runtime Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Tokio as its async runtime. It was chosen because it is the de facto standard async runtime in the Rust ecosystem and has extensive ecosystem support for libraries and integrations, which favors ecosystem compatibility and community momentum.
